    "notes": "<p>Semantic version2026.10.07-bd-prehistory-target has scientific checkpoint date October7,2026, Pacific time. Actual Zenodo publication time is recorded independently. The completed scientific source and release assets are pinned to GitHub commit 7fbde527a9031baccd1f04b7ce3e8b905b2fdf10.</p>\n<p>The first standalone replay remains recorded as failed: the preserved preparation cap receipt had31 checks, while the unchanged frozen verifier executed32. Both normal numerical routes passed before that packaging failure. Additive current receipts and the external helper reference were corrected; frozen source code, numerical gates and old receipts remain unchanged. The subsequent full normal/optimized replay and independent saved-output review pass.</p>\n<p>The new BD archive SHA256 is515548abbc33b032d21f33705035ab92d63a43416fcd6fd80fe230d8276f17d9. Its payload manifest SHA256 is1bb65ecadc6ea11b9ffc58c4e88021b82728bb3696f50a7941468b4428a1b83a; portable helper SHA256 is37df86c5850c71b8c8cc4cb1926dbf21a6e841ff42358a272e5eb2f6bf293c22. The frozen complete27-file inventory supplies every filename, size, MD5 and SHA256.</p>\n<p>The previous October3 literal Notes guard retains its historical HTML-serialization failure; its separately pinned reviewed representation passed. This edition uses its own frozen complete metadata contract, with exact structure/decoded HTML events and documented server vocabulary decorations. Saved metadata and all27 file pins must pass before publication; all four additions require complete content-stream MD5/SHA256 checks. Automatic GitHub-to-Zenodo archiving was not enabled.</p>\n<p>Literature review is bounded by network access and does not claim an exhaustive web search or newly verified2025-26 discovery. Selected private material contributed only methodological controls; no private archive contents are released.</p>",
